## Context

A panel review of docs/erg-manual.md (generated by `erg --help --all`) surfaced
incoherences between the manual, tickets/spec-erg-v1.md, pep-erg-v1.md, and the
Go implementation. This umbrella tracks the clean-up wave.

## Child tickets
- 0097: Fix trailing period in close.go Blocked-by log line (bug)
- 0098: Fix log-line enforcement contradiction in manual
- 0099: Manual — define store auto-discovery mechanism
- 0100: Manual — agent usability gaps (Blocked-by format, archive scope, close edge cases)
- 0101: Manual — prose cleanup (title case, version passive voice, idempotency)
- 0102: Spec — sync missing rules (slug truncation, Tags repeatability, folder/header semantics)
- 0103: PEP — sync additions (Tags header, closed-path criterion, archive→closed decision)

## Exit criteria
- [ ] All seven child tickets closed
- [ ] No contradiction between manual, spec, and PEP on format rules
- [ ] Manual is sufficient for an agent to operate erg without reading other docs
